{"author":{"id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","is_bot":false,"login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},"baseRefOid":"65e1f3e35d89ac753c08913532da02fdadc0a536","body":"This PR resolves issue #33306 and #33340\r\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-10T15:05:09Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:53Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Use base-10 logarithms in SCM closures for #33306","oid":"134e99e385a3235df6b8990f77e50de9b1954161"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-13T16:05:02Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Use log10 in Borishanskii HTC closure (#33306)","oid":"6981569c49875f89af855fb31da702a290fc7535"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-14T16:21:47Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"The old negative_htc_error case used wire_diameter=0.003 to try to force a non-physical Gnielinski HTC. After correcting the Cheng-Todreas logarithm to base 10, that geometry no longer reaches the HTC guard first; it instead drives the coupled solve into invalid mixing or negative enthalpy. The requested wire is also larger than the pin-to-pin gap for this benchmark geometry, so the input is invalid before any friction, mixing, or HTC closure should run.\n\nAdd an early SCMTriAssemblyMeshGenerator validation that requires pitch to exceed pin diameter and requires dwire to be no larger than pitch - pin_diameter. Use MOOSE's fuzzy floating-point comparison so benchmark geometries where dwire equals the pin-to-pin gap are accepted. Rename the regression test to invalid_wire_diameter_error and make it expect this geometry error directly.","messageHeadline":"Reject oversized wire diameters in subchannel mesh","oid":"e89b2982dc757b7af715a731db643bac174ad068"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-14T16:47:00Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"The sodium-19pin SFR tests used Gnielinski for the duct HTC closure while using Dittus-Boelter for the pins. With the HTC positivity guard active, the low-Pr sodium duct calculation can produce a non-physical Gnielinski HTC after the subchannel solve has converged, causing the explicit, implicit, and monolithic tests to exit with an error instead of reaching CSVDiff.\n\nSwitch the duct HTC closure in all three sodium-19pin inputs to Dittus-Boelter, matching the existing pin HTC closure. The successful duct closure choices produce identical reported coolant/pin temperatures for these tests because duct_heat_flux is zero, so Dittus-Boelter is the simplest viable closure already present in the inputs. Regenerate the corresponding CSV gold files from passing direct runs.","messageHeadline":"Use Dittus-Boelter duct HTC in sodium-19pin tests","oid":"e6880842b9f78cd1c94e53b84b22b1a917c11b07"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-14T16:54:39Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"The base-10 logarithm corrections change the wire-wrapped Cheng-Todreas friction/mixing response and the Borishanskii HTC result. The affected tests ran to completion but failed CSVDiff because their gold files still reflected the old natural-log behavior.\n\nRefresh the gold CSVs for the heat-transfer correlation cases, THORS blockage validation cases, ORNL-19, Toshiba-37, and the EBR-II SHRT-17 SFR problem using the outputs generated by the updated closures. This updates only baselines for tests whose numerical results changed because the intended closure formulas changed.","messageHeadline":"Regold subchannel log10 correlation outputs","oid":"6fa529f2d143c9f1076e2e2627fe627411f702d9"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-14T23:24:09Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Fix subchannel crossflow estimate indexing (#33340)","oid":"20b55adee0eb50f1c60c66df0deba67e025dfe00"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-16T17:16:05Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"Store the assembly bulk Reynolds number on the subchannel problem and use it for the Updated Cheng-Todreas transition regime and interpolation parameter. Regold affected outputs.","messageHeadline":"Use bulk Reynolds number for Cheng-Todreas transition","oid":"4e469e257c7f87a67428cde87acaecbcfd12cc4c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-16T17:44:34Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Use bulk Reynolds number for Cheng-Todreas mixing","oid":"d4a59a04b5217aedcbf598a690cd3822ea9b3969"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-06T16:03:00Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDM3MTUx","login":"GiudGiud","name":"Guillaume Giudicelli"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"…ngTodreas.md\n\nCo-authored-by: Guillaume Giudicelli <<email>>","messageHeadline":"Update modules/subchannel/doc/content/source/scmclosures/SCMMixingChe…","oid":"15c5de12b311333b48f72d1796baa267b693afcc"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-10T21:21:52Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"edit inputs and regold","oid":"ccec90f5a523561badadd9eafe56a8507afe62d4"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-10T22:48:19Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix singularity issue with zero massflow","oid":"ba2fb2eb364304dc8274c4f8f27471baa7bfdd87"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-11T15:42:28Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"regold heavy tests","oid":"6f700e0a73928b7c241a4000814276cb8f42a180"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-24T20:33:28Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"correct naming of closure model","oid":"64c0dbbd5739162491ad879254790d41f89b476a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-24T21:31:16Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"…ure PRs","messageHeadline":"parameterize coeffients used, so it will be easier to abstract in fut…","oid":"7b722f083ade6f723e62f215c8bc0087e5469ec1"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-24T21:38:11Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix LBE test","oid":"f4155f7757d547be045bcdb36fbb8d754a5ba1fd"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-25T00:34:05Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fix tiny dt test","oid":"dc30dd6ed2ce6d521eac7889a6321c8faf6cc57a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-10T16:14:57Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:55Z","messageBody":"Regenerate the THORS (FFM-3A, FFM-5B) and EBR-II steady-state (XX09_TTC,\nXX09_TTC45) validation figures via MooseDocs media script directives\ninstead of hand-maintained static images, following the pattern used by\nopen_pronghorn jet validation case. Scripts live under\nmedia_scripts/validation/<case>, mirroring the original validation\ndirectory layout. Transient EBR-II figures and cases without existing\nplotting scripts or data (AREVA FCTF, ORNL-19, Toshiba-37, PSBT,\nPNNL-12-pin) are left as static images per discussion.\n\nThe superseded static PNGs are removed from the large_media submodule\n(pointer bump included in this commit).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Automate subchannel V&V steady-state result plots","oid":"baf106bc57901b0ee4491fe7b4d4e37c219bcb0e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-10T16:18:40Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T17:51:55Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Update large_media pointer after rebasing onto upstream master","oid":"57539dbb1f262e2a4aa8a4618ad2b4f60bdabe98"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-10T16:33:01Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-10T21:20:23Z","messageBody":"…media-script review comments\n\nReformat plot5B.py and plot_results.py per black --config pyproject.toml to\nresolve CIVET Precheck failure. Also fix Re_b LaTeX typo in\nSCMFrictionUpgradedChengTodreas.md and move wire sweep/drag coefficient\nvariables to point-of-use as const Real in SCMFrictionUpgradedChengTodreas.C.\n\nRemove the checked-in PNGs under media_scripts/validation/ (THORS FFM-3A,\nFFM-5B_high, FFM-5B_low; EBR-II XX09_TTC, XX09_TTC45) -- these are generated\non-the-fly by their sibling plot scripts via the MooseDocs !media <script>.py\nmechanism at every doc build, so committing them is redundant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Fix black formatting for media scripts; address friction closure and …","oid":"0f06b2bff5aa279b3042175578dd040c5147bb17"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-11T21:40:41Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOBscmPw","login":"kyriv-lab","name":"Vasileios Kyriakopoulos"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-11T21:47:58Z","messageBody":"At low Prandtl numbers (e.g. liquid sodium, Pr ~ 0.005), the modified\nGnielinski correlation's denominator can cross zero once the friction\nfactor is large enough, producing unbounded or sign-flipped Nusselt\nnumbers. Floor the denominator at 0.1, flagging a solution warning\nwhen engaged, so Nu saturates near the flat, conduction-dominated\nbehavior the low-Pr flattening is meant to produce. Document the fix\nin the SCMHTCGnielinski doc page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"Floor Gnielinski correlation denominator to avoid low-Pr singularity","oid":"bc5b507d5c14595d5e96ab31fd2b1456904204ad"}],"files":[{"path":"large_media","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"modules/combined/test/tests/subchannel_thm_coupling/gold/THM_SCM_coupling_out.csv","additions":9,"deletions":9},{"path":"modules/combined/test/tests/subchannel_thm_coupling/gold/THM_SCM_coupling_out_subchannel0.csv","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"path":"modules/combined/test/tests/subchannel_thm_coupling/gold/THM_SCM_coupling_pump_out.csv","additions":3,"deletions":3},{"path":"modules/combined/test/tests/subchannel_thm_coupling/gold/THM_SCM_coupling_pump_out_subchannel0.csv","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"path":"modules/combined/test/tests/su